From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] ntdll, wow64: NtSetInformationFile leaves the status block alone on error

NtSetInformationFile wrote its IO status block even for a request that was
refused; on Windows an error status leaves the block alone (only a request
that goes through writes status and information).  Fourteen todo_wine
checks in ntdll's file.c test, written against Windows, record this for
renames onto existing names, links, completion ports, mailslots and more.
The error paths of Wine's NtSetInformationFile, and of the wow64 thunk
(which also wrote the block for the lengths and classes it refuses itself),
now leave the block untouched, and the todo_wine marks are removed.

